#
# can-utils "candump -l" text, 11-bit Quick identifiers.
#
# There is no J1939 header on these frames: the CAN ID is only a message type
# and becomes the PGN, and nothing reports a priority, destination or 8-bit
# source address, because an 11-bit identifier has no room for them. The
# 16-bit talker ID is payload and decodes as an ordinary field.
#
(1502979132.106111) vcan0 6C1#C1186B0000000200
(1502979133.206111) vcan0 6C0#C118010203040506
(1502979134.306111) vcan0 6C2#C118000000000000
#
# 0x123 is not a Quick message type we have reverse engineered. It must resolve
# to the catch-all entry and keep its payload as raw bytes, rather than being
# reported as whichever packet happens to be first in the table.
#
(1502979135.406111) vcan0 123#A1B2C3D4E5F60708
